  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "A first winter for someone from the tropics",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "This section isn't grammar. It's here because almost every newcomer from a warm country gets through their first December the same way: shocked, freezing, and wishing they'd bought the right boots."
        },
        {
          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "What you need before December",
          "items": [
            "**Тепла куртка** — a thick jacket, ideally down or synthetic fill. This is the one thing not to skimp on.",
            "**Шапка** — a knit hat that covers your ears. Not fashion but necessity: you lose a lot of body heat through your head.",
            "**Зимове взуття** — boots with rough soles. Kyiv's frozen sidewalks are more dangerous than the temperature.",
            "**Термобілизна** — thermal underwear. Ukrainians wear it without a second thought, and once you try it you'll understand why.",
            "⚠️ The sentence you need in the store: **Мені потрібна тепла куртка на зиму** — I need a warm jacket for the winter."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sub",
          "text": "Weather vocabulary"
        },
